{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3178","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3178","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3178\",\"parent_revision\":\"5fbb60f91bf5d8c9202f74718f5a40b2b1e72952b2dc2a94b0e34fcf7fe16791\",\"root_revision\":\"5fbb60f91bf5d8c9202f74718f5a40b2b1e72952b2dc2a94b0e34fcf7fe16791\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-23\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nTwo scripts remain runnable that would, if executed, reproduce the #3152 defect across the whole backlog and overwrite content the architecture designates as human-owned.\\n\\nScripts:\\n- `.claude/scripts/rebuild_issue_bodies.py`\\n- `.claude/scripts/repair_from_original_register.py`\\n\\nThree separate problems, each independently sufficient to cause damage:\\n\\n1. Title-derived Story synthesis. Both hold private copies of `ROLE_MAP` and `BENEFIT_MAP` (deleted from `models.py`) and build `## Story` as \\\"As a {role}, I want to {title.lower()} so that {benefit}\\\". This is the exact mechanism #3152 was filed for: an item title usually names an undesired current state, so slotting it into an \\\"I want to\\\" clause asserts a desire for the very thing the item exists to remove. PR #3160 removed this from the creation workflows; these two scripts were missed because a repo-wide grep for `ROLE_MAP` was truncated by 164KB of matches from `graphify-out/`.\\n\\n2. Mass overwrite of human-owned content. `rebuild_issue_bodies.py` iterates open issues and calls `issue.edit(body=...)`. `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` under \\\"GitHub writable records\\\" states that work-item issue bodies remain human-owned GitHub content and are never overwritten, with the `dh-work-item-version` comments serving as the append-only audit record instead. These scripts violate that directly.\\n\\n3. Stale source of truth. Both read `.claude/backlog/*.md`. That directory is an ignored local cache; this checkout's configured backend is GitHub Issues. So the scripts would overwrite authoritative remote content from a cache that may be arbitrarily out of date.\\n\\nA guard in `rebuild_issue_bodies.py` skips issues whose body already contains `## Story`. That guard becomes actively wrong once Story is no longer written at creation \u2014 it would then treat every correctly-formed item as needing rebuild.\\n\\nNeither script was executed during the incident. Both are listed as live tooling in `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog-tools-administrator/references/domain-registry.md` and `.claude/skills/backlog-tools-administrator/references/domain-registry.md`, so an agent following that registry could run them.\\n\\n`repair_from_original_register.py` additionally reads `.claude/original-backlog-register.md`, which no longer exists in the repo.\\n\\nImpact if left: any agent or human following the domain registry can rewrite every open issue body in the repository with fabricated Story sections, destroying groomed content and reproducing #3152 at scale.\\n\\nUser-provided context: whether these are one-shot migration scripts that have outlived their purpose and should be deleted, or tooling that should be repaired, is the open question \u2014 deletion was deliberately not attempted during the incident because it is destructive and was outside the requested scope.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Encountered during #3152 remediation, carried through the PR #3160 handoff, 2026-08-23\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-23\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"dcb48db0be5e51ad53931e69dae698375f3bab42d0278de85f2e8ff85808efae\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQPWrqQ\"}"}